+# XAM / bootanim runtime result
+
+Date: 2026-11-10
+
+## Implemented and verified
+
+- Added a PPC32 `sc` bridge to `CPU`.
+- Kernel import thunks now execute `li r0, ordinal; sc` rather than returning zero from a fake leaf stub.
+- The bridge preserves guest argument registers `r3-r10`, writes the service result to `r3`, and returns through the guest `LR`.
+- The bridge is installed on the primary CPU and propagated to secondary CPUs created by `PPCSimulator`.
+- Unknown kernel ordinals return `0xC0000002` (`STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`).
+- XAM and bootanim executable import thunks are installed from `imports.csv`.
+- XAM import ordinal 678 is looked up from the manifest (guest thunk `0x81A72344`).
+- `--xam` runs an emulator-only guest boot shim at `0x9FF00000`; it calls the actual XAM thunk via `bctrl`, dispatches `AniStartBootAnimation`, then transfers to XAM entrypoint `0x81696AF0`.
+- `bootanim.xex.pe` is mapped at `0x98000000`, its imports are installed, and the module is registered with the kernel service.
+- The XAM entrypoint reaches the configured thread-exit sentinel without the previous PC=0 exception.
+
+## Verified run
+
+Command:
+
+```sh
+java -Djava.awt.headless=true -cp build pcp.PCP --xam --headless --trace --max 100000 --png build/xam-bootanim-dispatch.png
+```
+
+Observed evidence:
+
+```text
+[TKERNEL] BOOTANIM REGISTERED base=98000000 size=00087000 entry=00000000 hasEntry=false
+[TKERNEL] AniStartBootAnimation accepted: bootanim image=98000000+00087000; kernel-managed image, no PE entrypoint
+[TKERNEL] DISPATCH ordinal=678 AniStartBootAnimation PC=81A72348 LR=9FF00010 r3=00000000
+PC=81696af0 insn=3b400001
+[CPU] Halt: 'b .' en PC=0x9ffc0010
+[headless] 213 instrucciones, PC=0x9ffc0010, halted=true
