+# Delivery: PPC32 kernel import dispatch / XAM animation request
+
+Updated project delivery for 2026-11-10.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `cpu/CPU.java`: system-call callback for PPC `sc`; service ID in `r0`, result in `r3`, return via `LR`.
+- `PPCSimulator.java`: propagates the kernel callback to primary and secondary CPU threads.
+- `xenon/TKernel.java`: executable import thunks dispatch to kernel services; unknown ordinals return `STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`; bootanim registration and XAM boot hook added.
+- `PCP.java`: `--xam` maps XAM and bootanim, installs imports, registers bootanim, and enters through the emulator-side boot hook.
+- `tests/run-xam-bootanim-dispatch-smoke.sh`: verifies ordinal 678 dispatch and XAM entry/exit.
+- `tests/run-xam-entry-smoke.sh`: now runs correctly in headless environments.
+
+## Execution result
+
+PASS: `./tests/run-all-smoke.sh`
+
+The XAM guest import thunk at `0x81A72344` executes `li r0,678; sc`. The bridge dispatches `AniStartBootAnimation`, returns to the guest shim, and the shim transfers to XAM entrypoint `0x81696AF0`. XAM reaches thread-exit sentinel `0x9FFC0010` after 213 instructions.
+
+## Not completed / no false claim
+
+`bootanim.xex.pe` is mapped at `0x98000000`, imports are installed, and the kernel registers it. The XEX/PE entrypoint is zero, its export directory has no exported functions, and its `.XBMOVIE` virtual section is zero-filled. The binary supplies no valid guest entrypoint. Thus this delivery does **not** claim to have executed bootanim's internal guest code or rendered the retail animation. PM4/Xenos command processing and real animation playback remain unimplemented. See `XAM-BOOTANIM-STATUS.md` and `README-KERNEL-IMPORT-DISPATCH.md`.
